From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guilherme Cardoso <luminoso@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: dsa: qca8k: add MAC_PWR_SEL voltage flags

MAC_PWR_SEL (0x00e4) on the QCA8337 selects 1.5V or 1.8V I/O for the
RGMII0 (MAC0) and RGMII1 (MAC5/MAC6) interfaces. The right setting
depends on how the board is wired. Add two flags so the device tree
can state it.

Link: https://github.com/openwrt/openwrt/issues/18979
Signed-off-by: Guilherme Cardoso <luminoso@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/dsa/qca8k.yaml |   13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/dsa/qca8k.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/dsa/qca8k.yaml
@@ -59,6 +59,19 @@ properties:
       using SW regs. The pin strappings related to LED open-drain mode are
       B68 on the QCA832x and B49 on the QCA833x.
 
+  qca,mac-pwr-sel-rgmii0-1p8v:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/flag
+    description:
+      Set the MAC0 RGMII interface to 1.8V in the MAC_PWR_SEL register. If
+      either qca,mac-pwr-sel-rgmii0-1p8v or qca,mac-pwr-sel-rgmii1-1p8v is
+      set, an interface without its property is set to 1.5V. If neither is
+      set, the register is left untouched.
+
+  qca,mac-pwr-sel-rgmii1-1p8v:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/flag
+    description:
+      Set the MAC5/6 RGMII interface to 1.8V in the MAC_PWR_SEL register.
+
   mdio:
     $ref: /schemas/net/mdio.yaml#
     unevaluatedProperties: false
